handDesc.handNote:
, 
Fifteenth-century script
Black, red.

The incipit lines of all texts, alternating with black lines, and the incipit lines of the inner sections of the texts; the caption of the miniature; 
    some of the marginal notes indicating liturgical occasions on which a given section should be recited; the subscriptiones of Leviticus, Judges and Ruth; 
    numerals; elements of the interpunction, text dividers and caesura signs, quire marks.

handNote.seg:
The incipit lines of all texts, alternating with black lines, and the incipit lines of the inner sections of the texts; the caption of the miniature; 
                               some of the marginal notes indicating liturgical occasions on which a given section should be recited; the subscriptiones of Joshua; 
                               numerals; elements of the interpunction, text dividers and caesura signs, quire marks.
